## If I had to pick three

1. **`run_triage.py`** (0.1) — unblocks measurement entirely, depends on nothing else.
2. **The firehose** (1.1) — gates re-harvesting, and the numbers point somewhere different
   from what §8 assumed.
3. **Label hygiene** (1.2) — cheap, and 10% of your borderline stratum is currently invisible
   to the metric that matters most.
